<div _ngcontent-ng-c343160584="" class="ng-tns-c343160584-1 chat-history"><div _ngcontent-ng-c343160584="" class="ng-tns-c343160584-1 ng-star-inserted"><!----><share-turn-viewer _ngcontent-ng-c343160584="" _nghost-ng-c3025034799="" class="ng-tns-c343160584-1 ng-star-inserted" id="f5a982b7f49a8e0e" style=""><div _ngcontent-ng-c3025034799="" class="share-turn-viewer ng-star-inserted"><user-query _ngcontent-ng-c3025034799="" _nghost-ng-c3843244048="" class="ng-star-inserted"><span _ngcontent-ng-c3843244048="" class="user-query-container right-align-content"><!----><user-query-content _ngcontent-ng-c3843244048="" class="user-query-container" _nghost-ng-c3253035101="" style="--max-lines-for-collapse-count: 5;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="user-query-container user-query-bubble-container ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="file-preview-container ng-star-inserted"><!----><!----><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-content ng-star-inserted" id="user-query-content-0" jslog="275422;track:impression,attention" data-hveid="0" decode-data-ved="1" data-ved="0CAAQ3ucQahcKEwiJhIuHxqmRAxUAAAAAHQAAAAAQBA"><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><button _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" mat-icon-button="" aria-label="Copy prompt" mattooltip="Copy prompt" class="mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-button-base mat-mdc-tooltip-trigger action-button mat-unthemed" mat-ripple-loader-uninitialized="" mat-ripple-loader-class-name="mat-mdc-button-ripple" mat-ripple-loader-centered="" aria-controls="user-query-content-0" jslog="273008;track:generic_click,impression;BardVeMetadataKey:[[&quot;r_f5a982b7f49a8e0e&quot;,&quot;c_912d96631775c152&quot;,null,null,null,null,null,null,1,null,null,null,1]];mutable:true"><span class="mat-mdc-button-persistent-ripple mdc-icon-button__ripple"></span><mat-icon _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" role="img" fonticon="content_copy" class="mat-icon notranslate gds-icon-m action-button-icon google-symbols mat-ligature-font mat-icon-no-color" aria-hidden="true" data-mat-icon-type="font" data-mat-icon-name="content_copy"></mat-icon><span class="mat-focus-indicator"></span><span class="mat-mdc-button-touch-target"></span></button><!----></div><!----><!----><span _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="user-query-bubble-with-background ng-star-inserted"><!----><span _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="horizontal-container"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" role="heading" aria-level="2" class="query-text gds-body-l" dir="ltr"><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> # idea process <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> ## idea 1 <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> You have effectively re-discovered the "Forward-Backward Slack" calculation (often attributed to Savelsbergh, 1992 in VRP literature). This is the standard industrial way to handle insertion heuristics because, as you noted, it allows for $O(1)$ or $O(N)$ feasibility checks instead of re-simulating the whole route. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Your intuition to decouple the "Trip Structure" (the order of stops) from the "Vehicle Assignment" (the specific timestamps) is the correct architectural move for optimization. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Here is how we formalize your ideas into the simulation. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> 1. The Slack Logic ($O(1)$ Insertion) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> You are correct: we do not need to run the full scheduler to check if a vehicle can take a trip. We only need to know if the vehicle's accumulated slack is large enough to accommodate the detour. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> For a vehicle with an existing route (sequence of stops) $S = (s_0, s_1, ..., s_n)$: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Earliest Arrival ($E_i$): Calculated forward from the current time. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> $$E_0 = t_{now}$$ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> $$E_{i} = \max(E_{i-1} + \tau_{i-1, i}, \ t^{earliest}_i)$$ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Latest Arrival ($L_i$): Calculated backward from the last stop. This represents the latest we can arrive at stop $i$ without making any subsequent stop $j &gt; i$ late. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> $$L_n = t^{deadline}_n$$ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> $$L_i = \min(t^{deadline}_i, \ L_{i+1} - \tau_{i, i+1})$$ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Maximum Shift (Slack) ($M_i$): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> $$M_i = L_i - E_i$$ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> The Linear Insertion Check: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> If you want to insert a new Trip segment (duration $\delta$) between stop $i$ and $i+1$, you just check: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> $$\delta \leq M_i$$ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> (Note: You also have to check that the new segment itself is feasible, but the check against the existing passengers becomes instantaneous). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> 2. Refining "Start Time based on Closest Vehicle" <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> "I think we can assume the start time of each trip to be the time it takes for the closest vehicle to get there." <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> This is a powerful pruning lower bound, but be careful not to make it a hard constraint for feasibility. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Logic: Let $t_{min\_arrival} = t_{now} + \min_{v \in V_{cand}} (\text{dist}(v, o_{trip}))$. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Usage: When building the GlobalTrip, you calculate the schedule starting at $t_{min\_arrival}$. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> The Constraint: If a trip is impossible starting at $t_{min\_arrival}$ (the earliest physically possible time), it is impossible for all vehicles. Discard it. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> The Warning: Do not "bake in" this start time. A vehicle that is further away might still be a valid candidate, provided it arrives before the request's latest pickup time ($t^p_r \leq t^r_r + \Omega$). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> 3. "Save All Schedules" -&gt; Storing Topologies <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> "I think we should save all schedules... because we might have to insert stops for current passengers later" <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> You are right. A "Trip" is not just a set of requests; it is a set of requests plus a topological order. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> For a trip with requests $\{A, B\}$, the valid topologies (orders) might be: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> $o_A \to o_B \to d_A \to d_B$ (FIFO) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> $o_A \to o_B \to d_B \to d_A$ (LIFO) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> If you only save #1 (the "optimal" one for an empty car), you might fail to match a vehicle that already has a passenger going near $d_B$ but needs to drop them off before $d_A$. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Refined Structure: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Store a GlobalTrip object that contains a list of ValidPermutations. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Proposed Implementation: The "Global Trip" Architecture <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Here is the Python structure that implements your "Linear Slack" and "Global Trip" ideas. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Python <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> from typing import List, Set, Dict, NamedTupleclass Stop: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     # A point in space-time (Pickup or Dropoff) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     location: int <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     deadline: float <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     is_pickup: bool <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     request_id: strclass RouteTopology: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     Represents ONE specific ordering of stops for a set of requests. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     Example: [Pickup A, Pickup B, Drop A, Drop B] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     Does NOT contain absolute timestamps, only relative constraints. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     def __init__(self, ordered_stops: List[Stop]): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         self.stops = ordered_stops <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # Pre-calculate static drive times between stops in this order <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         self.static_duration = self._calc_duration() <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # Calculate the "Internal Slack" of this topology alone <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # (Assuming start at t=0, how much can we delay internally?) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         self.max_internal_delay = self._calc_internal_slack()class GlobalTrip: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     Represents a SET of requests {r1, r2...}  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     and the Vehicles that can theoretically serve them. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     def __init__(self, requests: Set[Request], candidate_vehicles: Set[str]): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         self.requests = requests <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         self.candidate_vehicles = candidate_vehicles # The "Intersection" set <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # KEY: Store ALL valid topological orderings, not just the best one. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # For 2 requests, max 4 permutations. For 3, max 30-ish. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         self.valid_topologies: List[RouteTopology] = [] class LinearSlackChecker: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     Your 'Linear Time' Insertion Logic <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """    @staticmethod <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     def can_merge(vehicle: Vehicle, trip_topology: RouteTopology) -&gt; bool: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # 1. Get Vehicle's current 'Hard' schedule (onboard passengers) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # We assume onboard passengers have a fixed drop-off order  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # (or we allow minimal re-ordering, but fixed is faster). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         v_stops = vehicle.planned_stops  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # 2. Calculate Forward (Earliest) and Backward (Latest) times for Vehicle <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # This is O(N) where N is passengers on board (usually small, &lt;4) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         E = calc_earliest_arrivals(v_stops, start_time=now, start_loc=vehicle.loc) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         L = calc_latest_arrivals(v_stops) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # 3. Check Pruning (Distance) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # Time to get from vehicle to start of new trip <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         time_to_trip_start = dist(vehicle.loc, trip_topology.stops[0].location) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         if now + time_to_trip_start &gt; trip_topology.stops[0].deadline: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             return False <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # 4. The Merge Check <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # We are trying to append the new trip AFTER the vehicle's current pickups? <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # Or weave them?  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # SIMPLEST CASE: Vehicle drops off everyone, then does trip?  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # COMPLEX CASE (Ride-Pooling): We must weave. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # If weaving, we iterate through insertion points in v_stops. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # We check if (slack at insertion point) &gt;= (duration of new trip segment) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         return True # Placeholder <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> The "Weaving" Complexity <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Your idea "Insert the vehicles drop-off in linear time" implies the following scenario: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Vehicle has passenger $P_1$ (Dropoff $D_1$ remaining). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> New Trip has Request $R_2$ (Pickup $O_2$, Dropoff $D_2$). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> We want to check if order $O_2 \to D_1 \to D_2$ is valid. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> To make this truly fast, you treat the Vehicle's Current Path as a "Timeline with Holes" (Slack). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> If the Vehicle has 5 minutes of slack between now and $D_1$, and picking up $O_2$ takes a 3-minute detour, it fits. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Updated Algorithmic Steps for build_graph: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Global Trip Generation (Phase 1): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Iterate combinations of requests. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Filter using intersection(vehicles). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Compute and store ValidTopologies (start time = $t_{now} + \min\_dist$). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Output: A dictionary of feasible GlobalTrips. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Vehicle Assignment (Phase 2): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Iterate through GlobalTrips. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> For each candidate_vehicle in the trip: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Fast Check: Can vehicle reach Trip Start before Latest Pickup? <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Slack Check: Does the vehicle have enough max_shift (Slack) in its current schedule to absorb the extra travel time required by this trip? <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> If yes -&gt; Add edge to RTV graph. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> This approach effectively utilizes the Slack and Virtual Schedule concepts you proposed to minimize the number of calls to the expensive routing engine. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> ## idea 2 <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> This is the correct architectural alignment. By storing the Topologies (Permutations) inside the Global Trip (Combination), you effectively separate the "What" (the group of people) from the "How" (the sequence of stops). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> The Sub-trip Lemma (Apriori) remains a set-theoretic operation: if the group $\{A, B, C\}$ is valid, then $\{A, B\}$ must have been a valid group. It doesn't matter if $\{A, B\}$ was routed $A \to B$ or $B \to A$; as long as some valid way existed, the subset is valid. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Here is the updated RTVGraphBuilder and the necessary data structures. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> 1. Data Structures <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> We need a lightweight struct to hold the "Bytecode" of a route (the topology) and a container for the Global Trip. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Python <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> from dataclasses import dataclassfrom typing import List, Tuple, FrozenSet, Set@dataclassclass RouteTopology: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     Represents one valid topological sort of a trip. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     This is what we store in the GlobalTrip base. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     stops: Tuple[Stop, ...]      # The fixed sequence (P1, P2, D1...) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     total_duration: float        # Cost for this specific sequence <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     entry_node: int              # The first stop's location (for quick reachability check) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     earliest_start: float        # Absolute time lower bound (from virtual vehicle) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">      <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     # We can add slack info here later if needed@dataclassclass GlobalTrip: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     Represents a clique of requests. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     Contains ALL valid ways to route them (permutations). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     request_ids: FrozenSet[str] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     valid_topologies: List[RouteTopology] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> 2. The Updated RTVGraphBuilder <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> This implementation: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Prunes by RV-Intersection: A pair $\{A, B\}$ is only a candidate if some vehicle can reach both A and B. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Uses find_all_topologies: Stores every valid entry/sequence. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Applies Lemma on Sets: Checks subsets using frozenset keys. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Python <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> class RTVGraphBuilder(IRTVGraphBuilder): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     def __init__(self, route_planner: ISingleVehicleRoutePlanner): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         self._route_planner = route_planner <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     def build_graph( <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         self, <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         rv_graph: RVGraph, <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         vehicles: Set[VehicleAvailability], <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         requests: Set[Request], <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     ) -&gt; RTVGraph: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         rtv = RTVGraph() <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         req_map = {r.id: r for r in requests} <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         veh_map = {v.vehicle_id: v for v in vehicles} <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # Master storage: size -&gt; { frozenset(ids) : GlobalTrip } <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         global_trips: Dict[int, Dict[TripId, GlobalTrip]] = defaultdict(dict) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # --- PHASE 1: SIZE 1 (Single Requests) --- <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # A single request has exactly 1 topology: Pickup -&gt; Dropoff <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         for r in requests: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             stops = (Stop(r.origin_node, True, r.id), Stop(r.destination_node, False, r.id)) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # Calculate static duration or fetch from cache <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # duration = ...  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">              <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             topo = RouteTopology( <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 stops=stops,  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 total_duration=0.0, # Placeholder <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 entry_node=r.origin_node, <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 earliest_start=r.request_time <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             ) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">              <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             t_id = frozenset([r.id]) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             global_trips[1][t_id] = GlobalTrip(t_id, [topo]) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # --- PHASE 2: SIZE 2 (Pairs from RR/RV) --- <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         rr_candidates = set() <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # 1. Extract Candidates from RR Graph <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         for r1_id, neighbors in rv_graph.rr_edges.items(): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             for r2_id in neighbors: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 if r1_id &lt; r2_id:  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                     rr_candidates.add(frozenset([r1_id, r2_id])) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # 2. Validate Candidates <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         for t_id in rr_candidates: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # A. Reachability Pruning (RV Intersection) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # Only process if there is at least 1 vehicle that connects to BOTH <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             if not self._has_common_vehicle(t_id, rv_graph): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 continue <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # B. Generate All Topologies <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             topologies = self._generate_topologies(t_id, req_map) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">              <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             if topologies: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 global_trips[2][t_id] = GlobalTrip(t_id, topologies) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         logger.info(f"Size 2: {len(global_trips[2])} valid global trips.") <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # --- PHASE 3: EXPANSION (Size 3+) --- <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         MAX_SIZE = 4 <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         for k in range(3, MAX_SIZE + 1): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             prev_level = global_trips[k - 1] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             if not prev_level: break <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">              <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # Generate Candidates from (k-1) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             candidates = self._generate_candidates(prev_level, rv_graph) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">              <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             for t_id in candidates: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 # A. Sub-trip Lemma (Apriori) on SETS <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 # "Does every subset of size k-1 exist in prev_level?" <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 # Note: We don't care about the topologies here, just feasibility existence. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 if not self._passes_subtrip_lemma(t_id, prev_level): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                     continue <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 # B. Reachability Pruning <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 if not self._has_common_vehicle(t_id, rv_graph): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                     continue <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 # C. Generate All Topologies <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 topologies = self._generate_topologies(t_id, req_map) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 if topologies: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                     global_trips[k][t_id] = GlobalTrip(t_id, topologies) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             logger.info(f"Size {k}: {len(global_trips[k])} valid global trips.") <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # --- PHASE 4: ASSIGNMENT --- <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # Now we map the GlobalTrip objects (with their lists of perms) to vehicles <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         all_trips = [] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         for size in global_trips: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             all_trips.extend(global_trips[size].values()) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         for g_trip in all_trips: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # 1. Find Candidate Vehicles (Intersection) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             candidate_vehs = self._get_common_vehicles(g_trip.request_ids, rv_graph) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">              <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             for vid in candidate_vehs: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 vehicle = veh_map[vid] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 # 2. DAG / Slack Insertion <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 # We check IF the vehicle can accept ANY of the valid topologies <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 # The RoutePlanner now likely takes the list of topologies and checks constraints <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 # We iterate the pre-calculated topologies <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 for topo in g_trip.valid_topologies: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                      <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                     # Quick Check: Can vehicle reach entry node? <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                     # (This replaces the expensive part of the old check) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                     if not self._can_reach_entry(vehicle, topo): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                         continue <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                     # Detailed Check: Slack Insertion / DAG <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                     # This method uses the pre-calc topology vs vehicle slack <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                     res = self._route_planner.check_insertion(vehicle, topo) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                      <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                     if res.is_feasible: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                         rtv.add_rtv_edge(vid, g_trip.request_ids, cast(FeasibleRoute, res)) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                         # Optimization: If we just need *one* valid way to serve it, break? <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                         # Or do we want the absolute best topology for this specific vehicle? <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                         # Usually finding one valid insertion is enough to create the edge. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                         break  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         return rtv <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     # --- HELPER METHODS --- <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     def _generate_topologies(self, t_id: TripId, req_map) -&gt; List[RouteTopology]: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         Calls the Planner to find ALL feasible permutations for a Virtual Vehicle. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         reqs = {req_map[rid] for rid in t_id} <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # Virtual Vehicle setup (Lower Bound) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         sorted_reqs = sorted(reqs, key=lambda r: r.request_time) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         anchor = sorted_reqs[0] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         virtual_veh = VehicleAvailability( <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             vehicle_id="virtual", <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             available_at_node=anchor.origin_node, <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             available_from_time=anchor.request_time, <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             passengers_onboard=[],  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             remaining_stops_to_serve=(), <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             capacity=4 <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         ) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # New method on RoutePlanner that returns List[RouteTopology] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         return self._route_planner.find_feasible_topologies(reqs, virtual_veh) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     def _has_common_vehicle(self, t_id: TripId, rv_graph: RVGraph) -&gt; bool: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         """Returns True if Intersection(RV_edges) is not empty.""" <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # This is a fast 'bloom filter' style check <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         common = None <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         for rid in t_id: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             vehs = set(rv_graph.rv_edges.get(rid, {}).keys()) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             if not vehs: return False <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             if common is None: common = vehs <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             else: common &amp;= vehs <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             if not common: return False <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         return True <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     def _get_common_vehicles(self, t_id: TripId, rv_graph: RVGraph) -&gt; Set[str]: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         common = None <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         for rid in t_id: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             vehs = set(rv_graph.rv_edges.get(rid, {}).keys()) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             if common is None: common = vehs <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             else: common &amp;= vehs <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         return common or set() <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">      <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     def _passes_subtrip_lemma(self, t_id: TripId, prev_level_trips: Dict[TripId, GlobalTrip]) -&gt; bool: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         Standard Apriori Check: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         For trip {A,B,C}, check if {A,B}, {B,C}, {A,C} exist in prev_level. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         for rid in t_id: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             subset = t_id - {rid} <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             if subset not in prev_level_trips: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">                 return False <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         return True <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     def _can_reach_entry(self, vehicle: VehicleAvailability, topo: RouteTopology) -&gt; bool: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         Simple geometric/time prune.  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         Can vehicle get from current_loc to topo.entry_node before topo.earliest_start + offset? <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # Note: topo.earliest_start is usually the request time.  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # A vehicle can arrive later than that (up to max wait). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # This check should be permissive:  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # Arr_Time &lt;= Earliest_Req_Time + Max_Wait <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # We can use the 'Nuclear Cache' here for O(1) distance lookup <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         return True # Placeholder for logic <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Key Changes Summary <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> GlobalTrip Object: Now acts as a container for List[RouteTopology]. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Phase 2 &amp; 3 (Build): The loop logic generates candidates, checks the Lemma (does the set exist?), checks RV-Intersection (can anyone serve it?), and then asks the planner for All Topologies. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Phase 4 (Assign): The assignment loop iterates through the stored topologies inside the GlobalTrip. It uses _can_reach_entry as a fast filter before running the full Slack/DAG insertion check. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Reachability Pruning: Using _has_common_vehicle ensures we don't waste time generating topologies for a clique that sits in a "dead zone" where no single vehicle can reach all participants. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> ## idea 3 <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> This idea is genuinely brilliant. You have essentially reinvented the Incremental Precedence Graph (or Reachability Lattice). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Instead of storing "The Answers" (a list of 2,500 permutations), you store "The Rulebook" (a small graph of valid moves) and solve it Just-In-Time when the vehicle arrives. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Why this is "Beautiful" <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Memory: A list of 2,500 permutations for $k=4$ takes ~1 MB of RAM (struct overhead). A Graph of 8 nodes takes 64 bytes (an $8 \times 8$ bitmask or float matrix). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Speed: Extending the graph from size $k$ to $k+1$ is $O(k)$, not factorial. You just add 2 new nodes ($P_{new}, D_{new}$) and check connections to the existing $2k$ nodes. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Robustness: It implicitly handles all entry points. You don't need to decide "Top-K entries" because the graph is the map for every possible entry. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> The Architecture: "The Incremental Trip Graph" <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> 1. The Structure (The "Trip Graph") <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> For a Global Trip $T$ with requests $\{r_1, \dots, r_k\}$, the graph $G_T$ contains: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Nodes: $2k$ stops ($P_1, D_1, \dots, P_k, D_k$). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Edges: A directed edge $u \to v$ exists if and only if: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Time: Earliest_Arrival($u$) + Travel($u, v$) $\le$ Latest_Arrival($v$). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Logic: $u \neq v$. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> We store this as a simple Adjacency Matrix (or Dictionary). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> 2. The "Extend" Operation ($O(k)$) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> To build trip $T_{new} = T_{old} \cup \{r_{new}\}$: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Copy: Take the Adjacency Matrix of $T_{old}$. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Add Nodes: Add row/col for $P_{new}$ and $D_{new}$. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Add Edges (The reuse): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Check feasibility of $P_{new} \to \text{Every Old Node}$ (and vice versa). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Check feasibility of $D_{new} \to \text{Every Old Node}$ (and vice versa). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Add internal edge $P_{new} \to D_{new}$. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Preserve: We never re-check connections between old nodes (e.g., $P_1 \to D_2$). That knowledge is preserved from the previous step. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> 3. The "Virtual Check" (Sanity) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Before saving this new graph, we run a quick Path Existence Check (is there any path from a P-node to a D-node that visits everyone?). If the graph is disconnected or has no Hamiltonian path, we discard the trip. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> 4. The "Extract" (Assignment) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> When Vehicle $V$ considers this trip: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Link: Add temporary edges from $V_{loc} \to \text{All P-Nodes}$. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Solve: Run a tiny DFS/Dijkstra on this 8-node graph to find the optimal path. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Note: Since $N \le 8$, this is microsecond-fast. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Implementation <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Here is the GlobalTrip class redefined to use your Graph idea. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Python <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> @dataclassclass TripGraph: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     Implicitly represents ALL valid permutations for a set of requests. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     stops: List[Stop]                # The nodes (0..2k-1) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     adj_matrix: np.ndarray           # 2D array of travel times (inf if invalid) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">      <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     # We can also store a bitmask of 'Precedence' if we want to be fancy <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     # e.g. prerequisites[i] = bitmask of stops that MUST precede stop i <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     prerequisites: List[int]     @classmethod <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     def from_base(cls, base: 'TripGraph', new_req: Request, network) -&gt; 'TripGraph': <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         Efficiently extends an existing graph with 2 new stops. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         """ <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # 1. Setup New Nodes <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         p_stop = Stop(new_req.origin_node, True, new_req.id) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         d_stop = Stop(new_req.destination_node, False, new_req.id) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         new_stops = base.stops + [p_stop, d_stop] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         n_old = len(base.stops) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         n_total = n_old + 2 <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # 2. Expand Matrix (Copy old data) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # We assume matrix stores 'Travel Time' if valid, else infinity <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         new_mat = np.full((n_total, n_total), np.inf) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         new_mat[:n_old, :n_old] = base.adj_matrix <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # 3. Compute New Edges (The "Update" Step) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # We only check cross-terms between [Old Set] and [New Pair] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # Helper: Check valid transition u -&gt; v <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         def get_valid_time(u: Stop, v: Stop): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # 1. Static Graph Time <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             tt = network.get_travel_time(u.location, v.location) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # 2. Constraint Check (Loose bounds for Global Graph) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # Earliest(u) + tt &lt;= Latest(v) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             if u.earliest + tt &gt; v.latest: return np.inf <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             return tt <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # A. Old &lt;-&gt; New <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         for i in range(n_old): <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             old = base.stops[i] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">              <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # Old -&gt; P_new <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             new_mat[i, n_old] = get_valid_time(old, p_stop) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # P_new -&gt; Old <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             new_mat[n_old, i] = get_valid_time(p_stop, old) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">              <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # Old -&gt; D_new (Only if P_new visited? Precedence handled in Solver, not Graph Edge) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             new_mat[i, n_old+1] = get_valid_time(old, d_stop) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             # D_new -&gt; Old <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">             new_mat[n_old+1, i] = get_valid_time(d_stop, old) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">              <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # B. Internal New (P -&gt; D) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         new_mat[n_old, n_old+1] = get_valid_time(p_stop, d_stop) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # 4. Update Prerequisites <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # Old prereqs match indices <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         new_prereqs = list(base.prerequisites)  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # P_new has no internal prereqs (besides existing ones implicitly) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         new_prereqs.append(0)  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         # D_new requires P_new (index n_old) <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         new_prereqs.append(1 &lt;&lt; n_old)  <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">          <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">         return cls(new_stops, new_mat, new_prereqs)@dataclassclass GlobalTrip: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     id: FrozenSet[str] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     graph: TripGraph         # &lt;--- The lightweight graph <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted">     candidate_vehicles: Set[str] <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Why this is a Game Changer <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> You have solved the Memory Bottleneck. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Permutations List: Stores (P1, P2, D1, D2), (P2, P1, D1, D2), (P1, P2, D2, D1)... <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> This is redundant. You store the edge P1 -&gt; D1 hundreds of times. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Trip Graph: Stores P1 -&gt; D1 once. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> This allows you to scale to $k=5$ or $k=6$ easily because the graph grows linearly ($N^2$ edges), whereas permutations grow factorially. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Next Step: <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> You implement the TripGraph.from_base method. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> Then, in your RTVGraphBuilder, instead of _generate_topologies (which returned a list), you verify that new_graph.has_hamiltonian_path() (boolean). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> If True, you store the Graph. <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> When assigning, vehicle.find_path_on(trip.graph). <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> # task <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"> I have this idea I am working on an I am trying to figure out how we iteratively build the graph! I want you to help me refine this idea mathematically. Especially I want to think of the graph. Now remember a graph is only valid for a certain set of vehicles, and once the graph is only valid for one vehicle would could insert the vehicles stop nodes for further pruning! <!----><!----></p><p _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="query-text-line ng-star-inserted"><!----><br _ngcontent-ng-c3253035101="" class="ng-star-inserted"><!----></p><!----></div><!----><!----><!----></span></span><!----></div><!----><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----></user-query-content></span></user-query><!----><response-container _ngcontent-ng-c3025034799="" class="response-container ng-tns-c2587252621-2 reduced-bottom-padding ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c2587252621=""><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="response-container ng-tns-c2587252621-2 response-container-with-gpi ng-star-inserted" jslog="173900;track:impression,attention" data-hveid="0" decode-data-ved="1" data-ved="0CAAQzM4KahcKEwiJhIuHxqmRAxUAAAAAHQAAAAAQBQ"><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="response-container-header ng-tns-c2587252621-2 ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="response-container-header-controls ng-tns-c2587252621-2"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="ng-tns-c2587252621-2 tts ng-trigger ng-trigger-singleResponseEnter ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="single-draft-response-container ng-tns-c2587252621-2"><!----></div></div><!----><tts-control _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" _nghost-ng-c3197637580="" class="ng-tns-c2587252621-2 ng-trigger ng-trigger-singleResponseEnter ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3197637580="" class="response-tts-container ng-star-inserted" data-test-draft-id="rc_6af04645466e9e16" style="height: 4127px;"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3197637580="" data-test-id="disabled-tooltip" class="mat-mdc-tooltip-trigger tts-button-container mat-mdc-tooltip-disabled"><button _ngcontent-ng-c3197637580="" mat-icon-button="" class="mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-icon-button mat-mdc-button-base mat-mdc-tooltip-trigger tts-button mat-unthemed ng-star-inserted" mat-ripple-loader-uninitialized="" mat-ripple-loader-class-name="mat-mdc-button-ripple" mat-ripple-loader-centered="" aria-label="Listen" jslog="184512;track:generic_click,impression;BardVeMetadataKey:[[null,null,null,&quot;rc_6af04645466e9e16&quot;,null,null,&quot;en&quot;,null,1,null,null,1,0]];mutable:true"><span class="mat-mdc-button-persistent-ripple mdc-icon-button__ripple"></span><mat-icon _ngcontent-ng-c3197637580="" role="img" fonticon="volume_up" class="mat-icon notranslate icon-filled google-symbols mat-ligature-font mat-icon-no-color ng-star-inserted" aria-hidden="true" data-mat-icon-type="font" data-mat-icon-name="volume_up"></mat-icon><!----><!----><!----><!----><span class="mat-focus-indicator"></span><span class="mat-mdc-button-touch-target"></span></button><!----><!----></div><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c3197637580="" role="menu" class="mat-mdc-menu-trigger playback-speed-menu-trigger multi" aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false"><mat-menu _ngcontent-ng-c3197637580="" yposition="below" xposition="after" class=""><!----></mat-menu></div><!----></tts-control><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="response-container-header-status ng-tns-c2587252621-2"><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="response-container-header-processing-state ng-tns-c2587252621-2"></div></div><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="presented-response-container ng-tns-c2587252621-2" jslog="283401;track:impression,attention" data-hveid="2"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="avatar-gutter ng-tns-c2587252621-2 ng-star-inserted"><bard-avatar _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="avatar-component ng-tns-c1437199241-4 ng-tns-c2587252621-2 ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c1437199241=""><div _ngcontent-ng-c1437199241="" bardavataranimationscontroller="" class="bard-avatar ng-tns-c1437199241-4"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1437199241="" class="avatar-container ng-tns-c1437199241-4"><div _ngcontent-ng-c1437199241="" class="avatar avatar_primary ng-tns-c1437199241-4 ng-trigger ng-trigger-botAvatarScaleDown ng-star-inserted"><bot-logo _ngcontent-ng-c1437199241="" class="ng-tns-c1437199241-4 is-dark-mode" _nghost-ng-c1731379540="" style="--bot-logo-size: 32px; --bot-logo-icon-size: 18px; --bot-logo-text: #25B2D4; --bot-logo-bg: #00404E; --bot-logo-border: #00404E;"><!----><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1731379540="" class="bot-logo-text sidenav-style-updates ng-star-inserted" style=""> R <!----><!----></div><!----></bot-logo></div><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c1437199241="" lottie-animation="" class="avatar_spinner_animation ng-tns-c1437199241-4" style="opacity: 0; visibility: hidden;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="32" height="32" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" style="width: 100%; height: 100%; transform: translate3d(0px, 0px, 0px); content-visibility: visible;"><defs><clipPath id="__lottie_element_5"><rect width="32" height="32" x="0" y="0"></rect></clipPath><linearGradient id="__lottie_element_9" spreadMethod="pad" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><stop></stop><stop></stop><stop></stop><stop></stop><stop></stop></linearGradient><linearGradient id="__lottie_element_16" spreadMethod="pad" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><stop></stop><stop></stop><stop></stop></linearGradient><linearGradient id="__lottie_element_20" spreadMethod="pad" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><stop></stop><stop></stop><stop></stop></linearGradient><linearGradient id="__lottie_element_24" spreadMethod="pad" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><stop></stop><stop></stop><stop></stop></linearGradient><linearGradient id="__lottie_element_28" spreadMethod="pad" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><stop></stop><stop></stop><stop></stop><stop></stop><stop></stop></linearGradient><linearGradient id="__lottie_element_32" spreadMethod="pad" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x1="-16" y1="0" x2="16" y2="0"><stop offset="0%" stop-color="rgb(49,134,255)"></stop><stop offset="50%" stop-color="rgb(49,134,255)"></stop><stop offset="100%" stop-color="rgb(49,134,255)"></stop><stop offset="100%" stop-color="rgb(49,134,255)"></stop><stop offset="100%" stop-color="rgb(49,134,255)"></stop></linearGradient></defs><g clip-path="url(#__lottie_element_5)"><g transform="matrix(1,0,0,1,16,16)" opacity="1" style="display: block;"><g opacity="1" transform="matrix(1,0,0,1,0,0)"><path stroke="url(#__lottie_element_32)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" fill-opacity="0" stroke-miterlimit="4" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="2" d=" M-4.383999824523926,-14.347999572753906 C-2.996999979019165,-14.772000312805176 -1.524999976158142,-15 0,-15 C0,-15 0,-15 0,-15 C1.7100000381469727,-15 3.3540000915527344,-14.713000297546387 4.886000156402588,-14.1850004196167"></path></g></g><g style="display: none;"><g><path stroke="url(#__lottie_element_28)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" fill-opacity="0" stroke-miterlimit="4"></path></g></g><g style="display: none;"><g><path stroke="url(#__lottie_element_24)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" fill-opacity="0" stroke-miterlimit="4"></path></g></g><g style="display: none;"><g><path stroke="url(#__lottie_element_20)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" fill-opacity="0" stroke-miterlimit="4"></path></g></g><g style="display: none;"><g><path stroke="url(#__lottie_element_16)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" fill-opacity="0" stroke-miterlimit="4"></path></g></g><g style="display: none;"><g><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" fill-opacity="0" stroke-miterlimit="4"></path></g></g><g style="display: none;"><g><path stroke="url(#__lottie_element_9)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" fill-opacity="0" stroke-miterlimit="4"></path></g></g></g></svg></div></div></bard-avatar><!----><!----></div><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="response-container-content ng-tns-c2587252621-2"><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="bot-name gds-title-s ng-tns-c2587252621-2 ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="bot-name-text ng-tns-c2587252621-2"> Ride-Sharing </div><span _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="bot-name-ugc-label ng-tns-c2587252621-2 ng-star-inserted">Custom Gem</span><!----><bot-experiment-badge _ngcontent-ng-c2587252621="" class="ng-tns-c2587252621-2" _nghost-ng-c3108469367=""><!----></bot-experiment-badge></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><processing-state _ngcontent-ng-c3025034799="" class="extension-processing-state ng-tns-c1381173882-3 processing-state_after-response ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c1381173882="" hidden=""><div _ngcontent-ng-c1381173882="" class="ng-tns-c1381173882-3"><!----><!----><!----></div></processing-state><!----><!----><message-content _ngcontent-ng-c3025034799="" class="message-content ng-star-inserted" _nghost-ng-c793834718=""><div _ngcontent-ng-c793834718="" inline-copy-host="" class="markdown markdown-main-panel stronger enable-updated-hr-color" id="" aria-live="off" aria-busy="false" dir="ltr" style="--animation-duration: 600ms; --fade-animation-function: linear;"><p data-path-to-node="0">This is a sophisticated approach. You are effectively proposing to move from a <b>Permutation-based state space</b> (storing lists of stops) to a <b>Precedence-based state space</b> (storing a Reachability Matrix).</p><p data-path-to-node="1">This shift reduces the memory complexity from Factorial <span class="math-inline" data-math="O(k!)"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span><span class="mclose">!)</span></span></span></span></span> to Quadratic <span class="math-inline" data-math="O(k^2)"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0641em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span class="" style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>, which is massive for scaling.</p><p data-path-to-node="2">Here is the mathematical refinement of your <b>Iterative Trip Graph</b> and how to handle the <b>Vehicle Context</b> injection.</p><hr data-path-to-node="3"><h3 data-path-to-node="4">Part 1: The Global Trip Graph (Request-Centric)</h3><p data-path-to-node="5">Before we look at a specific vehicle, we build a graph <span class="math-inline" data-math="G"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span></span></span></span></span> representing the "Physics of the Request Set."</p><h4 data-path-to-node="6">1. Definitions</h4><p data-path-to-node="7">Let a trip <span class="math-inline" data-math="T"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1389em;">T</span></span></span></span></span> consist of <span class="math-inline" data-math="k"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span></span></span></span></span> requests. The set of stops is <span class="math-inline" data-math="N = \{O_1, D_1, \dots, O_k, D_k\}"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.109em;">N</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">O</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner">…</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">O</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span></span>.
Total nodes: <span class="math-inline" data-math="2k"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span></span></span></span></span>.</p><p data-path-to-node="8">We define the <b>Reachability Matrix</b> <span class="math-inline" data-math="M"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.109em;">M</span></span></span></span></span> as a <span class="math-inline" data-math="2k \times 2k"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7778em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">×</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span></span></span></span></span> matrix where:
$$ M_{ij} = \begin{cases}
\tau(i, j) &amp; \text{if transition } i \to j \text{ is valid} \
\infty &amp; \text{otherwise}
\end{cases} $$</p><h4 data-path-to-node="9">2. The Validity Condition (The Edge)</h4><p data-path-to-node="10">An edge <span class="math-inline" data-math="i \to j"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6595em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.854em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0572em;">j</span></span></span></span></span> exists (is valid) if and only if:</p><ol start="1" data-path-to-node="11"><li><p data-path-to-node="11,0,0"><b>Identity:</b> <span class="math-inline" data-math="i \neq j"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel"><span class="mrel"><span class="mord vbox"><span class="thinbox"><span class="rlap"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="inner"><span class="mord"><span class="mrel"></span></span></span><span class="fix"></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mrel">=</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.854em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0572em;">j</span></span></span></span></span>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="11,1,0"><b>Precedence (Hard):</b> If <span class="math-inline" data-math="i = O_x"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6595em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">O</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">x</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="math-inline" data-math="j = D_x"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.854em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0572em;">j</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">x</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, valid. If <span class="math-inline" data-math="i = D_x"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6595em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">x</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and <span class="math-inline" data-math="j = O_x"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.854em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0572em;">j</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">O</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">x</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, <b>invalid</b> (you cannot drop off before you pick up).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="11,2,0"><b>Time Windows (Loose Bounds):</b>
</p><div data-path-to-node="11,2,1"><div class="math-block" data-math="E_i + \tau(i, j) \le L_j"><span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0576em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">τ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0572em;">j</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≤</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0572em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div><ul data-path-to-node="11,2,2"><li><p data-path-to-node="11,2,2,0,0"><span class="math-inline" data-math="E_i"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0576em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (Earliest Departure from <span class="math-inline" data-math="i"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6595em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span></span></span></span></span>): The earliest physically possible time a vehicle could leave node <span class="math-inline" data-math="i"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6595em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span></span></span></span></span>.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="11,2,2,1,0"><span class="math-inline" data-math="L_j"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">L</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0572em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (Latest Arrival at <span class="math-inline" data-math="j"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.854em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0572em;">j</span></span></span></span></span>): The absolute latest time node <span class="math-inline" data-math="j"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.854em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0572em;">j</span></span></span></span></span> can be visited (request time + max wait/delay).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="11,2,2,2,0"><span class="math-inline" data-math="\tau(i, j)"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">τ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0572em;">j</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>: Travel time between locations.</p></li></ul></li></ol><h4 data-path-to-node="12">3. The Iterative Build (The Induction)</h4><p data-path-to-node="13">We assume we have a valid matrix <span class="math-inline" data-math="M^{old}"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8491em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.109em;">M</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8491em;"><span class="" style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">o</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0197em;">l</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">d</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> for requests <span class="math-inline" data-math="R = \{r_1 \dots r_{k-1}\}"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0077em;">R</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">r</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner">…</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">r</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span><span class="mbin mtight">−</span><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span></span>. We add request <span class="math-inline" data-math="r_k"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5806em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">r</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (nodes <span class="math-inline" data-math="O_k, D_k"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">O</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">D</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>).</p><p data-path-to-node="14"><b>The Algorithm:</b></p><ol start="1" data-path-to-node="15"><li><p data-path-to-node="15,0,0"><b>Expand:</b> Create a new matrix <span class="math-inline" data-math="M^{new}"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.109em;">M</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6644em;"><span class="" style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">e</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0269em;">w</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> of size <span class="math-inline" data-math="(2k \times 2k)"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">×</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">2</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>. Copy <span class="math-inline" data-math="M^{old}"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8491em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.109em;">M</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8491em;"><span class="" style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">o</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0197em;">l</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">d</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> into the top-left block.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="15,1,0"><b>Cross-Check (The <span class="math-inline" data-math="O(k)"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span> Step):</b>
For every existing node <span class="math-inline" data-math="u \in N_{old}"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5782em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">∈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.109em;">N</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">o</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0197em;">l</span><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">d</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>:</p><ul data-path-to-node="15,1,1"><li><p data-path-to-node="15,1,1,0,0">Check <span class="math-inline" data-math="u \to O_k"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">O</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0278em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.0315em;">k</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>: Is <span class="math-inline" data-math="E_u + \tau(u, O_k) \le L_{O_k}"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0576em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span class="" style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0576em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">u</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span class=""></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.1132em;">τ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">u</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0278em;">O</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="